Joining the Royal Archer Team
How collaborators may participate, contribute, and grow with the project
Royal Archer welcomes thoughtful contributors who resonate with our mission of elevating stories, supporting writers, and building tools that serve creativity and clarity.

This document explains how you may join the project, what participation looks like, and what is required before becoming part of the team.

1. You Are Welcome to Explore, Fork, and Reuse the Files
You may:

fork this repository

copy and paste files into your own repository

adapt them for your own projects

as long as you:

credit Royal Archer Editorial Studio

link back to the original repository

respect the MIT License

accept the supplemental terms in COLLABORATION‑TERMS.md

Copying or reusing the files does not make you a member of the Royal Archer team.
It simply means you are using the open‑source materials responsibly.

2. How to Join the Team (Clear, Step‑by‑Step)
Joining the Royal Archer team is a collaborative process, not an automatic action.

Here is the correct pathway:

Step 1 — Explore the Project
Read:

README.md

CONTRIBUTING.md

COLLABORATION‑TERMS.md

CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md

This ensures alignment with the mission and values.

Step 2 — Communicate Your Interest
Open an Issue or Discussion introducing yourself:

who you are

what you’d like to contribute

your skills or background

your goals

This begins the conversation.

Step 3 — Make Meaningful Contributions
Examples:

improving documentation

submitting pull requests

offering editorial or writing support

contributing code or tools

helping with design or structure

Consistent, thoughtful contributions show commitment.

Step 4 — Align With the Mission
Royal Archer values:

clarity

kindness

craftsmanship

integrity

collaboration

respect for creative work

Team members must uphold these values.

Step 5 — Invitation to Join
Team membership is not automatic.

A contributor may be invited to join the team after:

demonstrating consistent contribution

showing alignment with the mission

communicating respectfully

building trust

accepting the collaboration terms

Formal team membership is granted only through direct communication with the project owner.

Step 6 — Co‑Ownership (Optional, Future Stage)
Co‑ownership requires:

long‑term contribution

shared vision

trust

a separate written agreement

It is never automatic.

3. What Team Membership Means
Team members may:

participate in planning

help shape the platform

collaborate on editorial or technical work

contribute to long‑term vision

take on leadership roles

Team membership does not grant ownership unless a separate agreement is signed.

4. What Team Membership Does NOT Mean
Joining the team does not:

grant automatic co‑ownership

grant financial rights

grant authority over the project

occur by copying files

occur by forking the repository

occur without communication

Royal Archer remains under the stewardship of Galina B. Nelson.

5. Thank You
If you are reading this, you are already part of the creative circle surrounding Royal Archer.
Whether you contribute code, ideas, writing, design, or simply encouragement — your presence matters.
Introduce yourself. Tell me your story!

We build this together, with care.

Galina B. Nelson @Galyushka
